# Shader sources are byte-compared against in-repo generators (e.g. the Bisqwit
# WGSL drift test `shared_bisqwit_wgsl_matches_generator`). Force LF on every
# platform so a Windows autocrlf checkout can't turn the committed file into CRLF
# and break that strict equality. WGSL/GLSL line endings are not semantic.
*.wgsl text eol=lf
*.glsl text eol=lf

# Rust sources are LF on every platform for the same reason (v2.9.8). The
# frontend's source-shape tests read `app.rs` through `include_str!` and split
# off the test module on "\n#[cfg(test)]\nmod tests {". A CRLF checkout -- the
# default on the windows-latest runner -- matches no split, so the tests then
# search their own text: `every_load_path_installs_a_dual_system_cabinet` found
# `self.build_dual_cabinet(` 3 times instead of 1 and failed main's CI on
# Windows only, after passing every PR run (PRs test Linux only). Every `.rs`
# file is already LF in the index (`git ls-files --eol`: 523 of 523), so this
# changes no committed byte; it fixes what a Windows checkout writes.
*.rs text eol=lf
